# Implementation Plan: Sovereign UI Stability & Security

The `sovereign-ui` project is currently experiencing React runtime errors due to matching its dependencies with the root project and missing local definitions for `framer-motion`. Additionally, a CSP warning needs to be addressed for Electron compliance.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> I am downgrading `sovereign-ui` from React 19 to React 18.3.1 to ensure consistency with the root project's extensive ecosystem and to resolve "Invalid Hook Call" errors.

## Proposed Changes

### [Component: sovereign-ui]

#### [MODIFY] [package.json](file:///c:/Users/ferna/Downloads/appforge-main/sovereign-ui/package.json)
- Downgrade `react` and `react-dom` to `18.3.1`.
- Add `framer-motion` to dependencies local to the project.
- Align `@types/react` and `@types/react-dom` to `^18.3.0`.

#### [MODIFY] [index.html](file:///c:/Users/ferna/Downloads/appforge-main/sovereign-ui/index.html)
- Add a Content Security Policy (CSP) meta tag to address Electron security warnings.

### [Component: Electron]

#### [MODIFY] [electron-main.cjs](file:///c:/Users/ferna/Downloads/appforge-main/scripts/electron-main.cjs)
- (Optional) Refine security settings in `webPreferences`.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Verification
- Run `npm install` in `sovereign-ui`.
- Start the unified launcher [LAUNCH_SOVEREIGN_CORE.bat](file:///c:/Users/ferna/Downloads/appforge-main/scripts/launchers/LAUNCH_SOVEREIGN_CORE.bat).
- Check Electron console for React "Invalid Hook" errors.
- Confirm CSP warning is resolved.
